    "text": "Let the sum of an infinite <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">G</mi><mo>.</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">P</mi><mo>.</mo></math>, whose first term is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>a</mi></math> and the common ratio is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>r</mi></math>, be <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>5</mn></math>. Let the sum of its first five terms be <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>98</mn><mn>25</mn></mfrac></math>. Then the sum of the first <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>21</mn></math>&nbsp;terms of an <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>AP</mi></math>, whose first term is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>10</mn><mi>a</mi><mi>r</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi>n</mi><mi>th</mi></msup></math>&nbsp;term is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></math>&nbsp;and the common difference is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>10</mn><msup><mo mathvariant=\"italic\">ar</mo><mn>2</mn></msup></math>, is equal to",
